{"A":"Own the serial sorting/correctness branch. Preserve bytewise strcmp-style token ordering, not numeric conversion. Replace equal-capacity first-character buckets and insertion sort with a generic full-token radix/counting design using unsigned bytes and safe dynamic storage; handle duplicate and skewed prefixes without relying on offset, bucket count, or balance. Validate exact line output and all-token permutation.","B":"Own the 4-core parallel-sort branch. Use parallel per-pass local histograms, global prefix offsets, and disjoint stable scatter buffers; avoid races, false sharing, and concurrent stdout writes. Do not parallelize the existing buckets, since skew defeats load balance. Keep a serial fallback when synchronization overhead is not justified, and demonstrate an end-to-end win rather than assuming fourfold speedup.","C":"Own I/O and memory-layout research. Investigate buffered token parsing and buffered ordered emission to replace per-item formatted I/O while preserving spelling, leading zeros, whitespace-delimited input behavior, and one output token per line. Use overflow-safe contiguous/resizable storage and pair it only with a nonquadratic sort. Measure I/O versus sorting costs; do not specialize to declared sample sizes or parse tokens as numbers.","G":"Integrate only compatible, validated candidates. Compare standalone A, A plus C, B, and B plus C under the same existing measurement setup; integrations may regress, so retain the fastest valid whole program, not every optimization. Check lexical monotonicity, permutation preservation, duplicates, skewed leading bytes, and exact stdout. Do not change the oracle, tests, compiler/toolchain, target, budgets, or permissions.","analysis":"The only measurement is a correct 4-case baseline averaging 0.414967 s, with no profiling or candidate evidence. Source behavior sorts strings via strcmp, while its fixed equal bucket slices can overflow under skew and its per-bucket insertion sort is quadratic; formatted input/output may also matter. ARM64 provides four CPU cores and no GPU, so prioritize robust radix sorting and buffered I/O, then admit parallelism only if measured end-to-end. No role may hardcode answers or omit valid inputs."}